@using Ecnanib.Agents

@*
    What the states of an agent mean, as a list (NFR-USA-2): each state by its word, with what
    it means beside it. A page that shows the states of several agents, or of one agent over
    time, writes the list under them, so that a state is explained where it appears. A page
    that shows one state says what it means beside the state itself. The page gives the list
    its heading, at the level that the page has there. Its texts are in AgentPages, and its
    look in app.css.
*@

<dl class="agent-states">
    @foreach (var state in States)
    {
        <dt>@AgentPages.Describe(state)</dt>
        <dd>@AgentPages.Explain(state)</dd>
    }
</dl>

@code {
    /// <summary>The states that the list explains, in their order. Every state, where a page says none.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<AgentState> States { get; set; } = Enum.GetValues<AgentState>();
}
